# Files and folders excluded from `gcloud builds submit` tarballs.
#
# The default tarball is the entire repo (30k+ files, >1 GiB here) because
# `gcloud` has no way to know which parts a given Dockerfile actually needs.
# Trimming this list down to only what the backend OR frontend Dockerfile
# reads cuts upload time by ~10x and stops the Cloud Build storage bucket
# from accumulating a revision per file tree.
#
# Format matches .gitignore. Keep it in sync when new heavyweight dirs land.

# --- Git metadata (hundreds of MB of object history) ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Python local envs + caches ---
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/

# --- Node / Next.js ---
# node_modules is ~500 MB and is fully rebuilt inside the Docker image
# via `npm ci` — never needs to cross the wire.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.turbo/
**/out/
**/build/
**/coverage/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Editor / OS artefacts ---
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Env files: secrets live in Secret Manager; never ship via build context. ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.local.example
!**/.env.example

# --- Docs, research, prototypes — none of these are imported at runtime. ---
# Everything under Temp/ (proposal PDFs, architecture image, tracking doc)
# and Prototyping/ (validation notebooks + fixtures) is reference material.
Temp/
Prototyping/

# --- Backend dev-only dirs not needed at build time ---
backend/logs/
backend/testing/
# tests are kept for now so CI can run pytest in future; flip to `tests/` to exclude.

# --- Local Docker dev artefacts ---
docker-compose.override.yml

# --- Large binary blobs that shouldn't live in git anyway ---
*.iso
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
!**/uv.lock
